  project's own rule: "Field names in the response are part of the contract; changes go through a versioned endpoint."
  The consistency argument is real — [38;5;153m/orders[39m already returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m — but consistency is what the versioned endpoint is
  for.

  The iOS clients are the sharp edge: shipped app versions can't be redeployed in step with the server.

